# font.bend — font8x8_basic by Daniel Hepper, public domain.
# Generated by tools_gen_font_list.py — do not hand-edit.
# font_byte(tbl, idx): idx = code*8 + row (0..1023) -> bitmap byte (U32).
# Bit 0 = leftmost pixel of the row (LSB-first, the font8x8 convention).
#
# The 1024 bytes live in a List<U32> (16 chunks of 64 cells). A previous
# version used 4x256-arm U32 matches; Bend 2.0.18's native C codegen needs
# ~9MB RAM per match arm (measured 2026-09-20: 1x256 arms = 2.3GB peak,
# 4x256 arms = SIGKILL at 4.8GB), so match-based tables cannot go native.
# font_data() builds the table once; callers thread it through.

